1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:05,786
Three thousand years ago, on a dusty road outside Jerusalem, an ox stumbles.

2
00:00:05,786 --> 00:00:06,646
A cart tips.

3
00:00:06,646 --> 00:00:11,525
A man named Uzzah reaches out to steady the sacred chest it carries.

4
00:00:11,525 --> 00:00:15,400
And according to the Bible, he falls dead on the spot.

5
00:00:15,866 --> 00:00:20,635
For two hundred years, people have offered a startling explanation.

6
00:00:20,635 --> 00:00:22,058
Not divine judgment.

7
00:00:22,058 --> 00:00:22,912
Electricity.

8
00:00:22,912 --> 00:00:26,400
The Ark of the Covenant, they say, was a machine.

9
00:00:26,866 --> 00:00:33,467
In nineteen sixty-eight, Erich von Däniken wrote: undoubtedly the Ark was electrically charged.

10
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:39,651
Rebuild it from the instructions of Moses, he claimed, and you get several hundred volts.

11
00:00:39,651 --> 00:00:41,666
Hollywood took it from there.

12
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:44,385
So we will treat it like evidence.

13
00:00:44,385 --> 00:00:45,643
A chain of custody.

14
00:00:45,643 --> 00:00:52,333
Follow the object from the day it was made to the day it vanished, and log every claim along the way.

15
00:00:52,799 --> 00:00:54,162
One promise first.

16
00:00:54,162 --> 00:01:02,715
This object is sacred to Jews and Christians, honored in Islam, and guarded, Ethiopia's church says, to this day.

17
00:01:02,715 --> 00:01:05,061
We are testing a modern theory.

18
00:01:05,061 --> 00:01:06,499
Not anyone's faith.

19
00:01:10,966 --> 00:01:11,678
Entry one.

20
00:01:11,678 --> 00:01:12,533
Mount Sinai.

21
00:01:12,533 --> 00:01:17,161
The book of Exodus, chapter twenty-five, gives the specification.

22
00:01:17,161 --> 00:01:19,866
And it reads almost like a work order.

23
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:26,118
A chest of acacia wood, two and a half cubits long, a cubit and a half wide and high.

24
00:01:26,118 --> 00:01:30,133
Roughly one hundred thirty by eighty by eighty centimeters.

25
00:01:30,599 --> 00:01:33,585
Overlaid with pure gold, inside and out.

26
00:01:33,585 --> 00:01:35,824
A gold molding around the top.

27
00:01:35,824 --> 00:01:44,333
Four gold rings at its feet, and two poles of acacia covered in gold, slid through the rings, never to be removed.

28
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:48,899
Then the lid, called the mercy seat, made of solid gold.

29
00:01:48,899 --> 00:01:53,658
On it, two cherubim facing each other, wings spread over the top.

30
00:01:53,658 --> 00:01:56,733
Inside, the stone tablets of the covenant.

31
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,442
And one line that theorists love.

32
00:01:59,442 --> 00:02:05,900
God tells Moses: there I will meet with you, and speak with you, from between the two cherubim.

33
00:02:06,366 --> 00:02:08,739
Read it as an engineer, they say.

34
00:02:08,739 --> 00:02:12,262
Two layers of gold, separated by insulating wood.

35
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:13,700
That is a capacitor.

36
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,360
The winged figures are the terminals.

37
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,158
And a voice between them?

38
00:02:18,158 --> 00:02:18,733
A radio.

39
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:21,235
First surprise in the file.

40
00:02:21,235 --> 00:02:23,949
This idea is not from the space age.

41
00:02:23,949 --> 00:02:31,186
The Leyden jar, the first device to store electric charge, was invented in seventeen forty-five.

42
00:02:31,186 --> 00:02:35,333
Within decades, German scholars compared it to the Ark.

43
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:40,296
The physicist Georg Christoph Lichtenberg drew the comparison.

44
00:02:40,296 --> 00:02:48,999
In seventeen ninety-seven, a writer named Lazarus Bendavid published the full claim: the Ark was a very good Leyden jar.

45
00:02:48,999 --> 00:02:51,899
The theory is older than the light bulb.

46
00:02:52,366 --> 00:02:53,944
Log one more detail.

47
00:02:53,944 --> 00:03:00,727
Deuteronomy tells the story again, and there Moses simply makes an ark of acacia wood.

48
00:03:00,727 --> 00:03:02,699
No gold mentioned at all.

49
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:03,819
Entry two.

50
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:04,471
The march.

51
00:03:04,471 --> 00:03:12,433
For forty years in the wilderness, the Ark travels ahead of the people, carried on the shoulders of Levites, by its poles.

52
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:19,965
At the river Jordan, the book of Joshua says the water stopped flowing the moment the priests' feet touched it.

53
00:03:19,965 --> 00:03:22,066
The people crossed on dry ground.

54
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:27,638
At Jericho, the Ark is carried around the city once a day for six days.

55
00:03:27,638 --> 00:03:29,938
On the seventh day, seven times.

56
00:03:29,938 --> 00:03:34,899
Seven priests blow rams' horns, the people shout, and the wall falls.

57
00:03:35,366 --> 00:03:37,649
Theorists read this as a weapon.

58
00:03:37,649 --> 00:03:43,000
A sonic device, or a power source that knocked down walls and parted water.

59
00:03:43,466 --> 00:03:45,813
But look at who acts in the text.

60
00:03:45,813 --> 00:03:48,302
The Ark does not glow, hum or fire.

61
00:03:48,302 --> 00:03:49,298
It is carried.

62
00:03:49,298 --> 00:03:55,344
The trumpets are rams' horns, the shout comes from people, and the story credits God.

63
00:03:55,344 --> 00:03:57,833
There is no mechanism here to test.

64
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,145
Entry three.

65
00:03:59,145 --> 00:03:59,849
Captivity.

66
00:03:59,849 --> 00:04:01,752
First Samuel, chapter four.

67
00:04:01,752 --> 00:04:08,304
Israel carries the Ark into battle against the Philistines, hoping it will guarantee victory.

68
00:04:08,304 --> 00:04:09,009
They lose.

69
00:04:09,009 --> 00:04:10,700
And the Ark is captured.

70
00:04:11,166 --> 00:04:15,969
The Philistines put it in the temple of their god Dagon at Ashdod.

71
00:04:15,969 --> 00:04:21,063
The next morning, the statue of Dagon lies on its face before the Ark.

72
00:04:21,063 --> 00:04:22,519
They set it back up.

73
00:04:22,519 --> 00:04:25,866
The next morning it is down again, and broken.

74
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:29,589
Then the people of Ashdod are struck with tumors.

75
00:04:29,589 --> 00:04:31,715
Rodents spread through the land.

76
00:04:31,715 --> 00:04:36,433
The Ark is moved to Gath, then to Ekron, and the affliction follows it.

77
00:04:36,899 --> 00:04:40,362
For the machine theory, this is radiation sickness.

78
00:04:40,362 --> 00:04:44,300
A dangerous energy source, poisoning everyone who kept it.

79
00:04:44,766 --> 00:04:47,075
But the text gives its own clues.

80
00:04:47,075 --> 00:04:49,313
Tumors that spread with rodents.

81
00:04:49,313 --> 00:04:51,552
Many readers see bubonic plague.

82
00:04:51,552 --> 00:04:58,407
After seven months the Philistines send it back with golden tumors and golden mice as an offering.

83
00:04:58,407 --> 00:05:00,366
Ancient ritual, not physics.

84
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:05,727
At Beth Shemesh, men look inside the Ark, and seventy are struck down.

85
00:05:05,727 --> 00:05:08,104
The lesson is the same every time.

86
00:05:08,104 --> 00:05:09,643
This object has rules.

87
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:12,300
Break them, and holiness strikes back.

88
00:05:12,766 --> 00:05:13,666
Entry four.

89
00:05:13,666 --> 00:05:15,465
The road to Jerusalem.

90
00:05:15,465 --> 00:05:22,580
The Ark rests for twenty years at Kiriath Jearim, in the house of a man named Abinadab.

91
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,933
His son Eleazar is set apart to guard it.

92
00:05:26,399 --> 00:05:29,654
Then King David comes to bring it to Jerusalem.

93
00:05:29,654 --> 00:05:31,524
With music and celebration.

94
00:05:31,524 --> 00:05:38,033
But they put it on a brand-new cart, pulled by oxen, the way the Philistines had sent it back.

95
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,819
The oxen stumble.

96
00:05:39,819 --> 00:05:41,991
Uzzah takes hold of the Ark.

97
00:05:41,991 --> 00:05:43,388
He dies beside it.

98
00:05:43,388 --> 00:05:48,199
David names the place Perez Uzzah, the outburst against Uzzah.

99
00:05:48,666 --> 00:05:52,119
Here the machine theory makes its strongest case.

100
00:05:52,119 --> 00:05:56,205
A man touches a gold-covered box and drops dead instantly.

101
00:05:56,205 --> 00:06:00,433
To an electrical engineer, it looks like a lethal discharge.

102
00:06:00,899 --> 00:06:09,072
An eighteen ninety-four article in the Electrical Review called the Ark a very expensive but very perfect Leyden jar.

103
00:06:09,072 --> 00:06:18,433
But to make it work, the writer added things the Bible never says: a fire burning on top, and golden lightning poles fifty yards high.

104
00:06:18,899 --> 00:06:20,554
And the text has a rule.

105
00:06:20,554 --> 00:06:25,791
In Numbers, the Ark is carried by Levites, on their shoulders, by the poles.

106
00:06:25,791 --> 00:06:27,377
Never touched directly.

107
00:06:27,377 --> 00:06:29,100
The cart was the mistake.

108
00:06:29,566 --> 00:06:32,755
Now the detail that hurts the electric theory.

109
00:06:32,755 --> 00:06:39,409
After Uzzah, the Ark stays three months in the house of Obed Edom, and his household is blessed.

110
00:06:39,409 --> 00:06:43,776
Then Levites carry it into Jerusalem by its gold-covered poles.

111
00:06:43,776 --> 00:06:46,133
People lived with it, and held it.

112
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,406
Entry five.

113
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:48,798
The Holy of Holies.

114
00:06:48,798 --> 00:06:57,374
King Solomon builds the Temple, and the Ark is placed in its innermost room, beneath the wings of two great cherubim.

115
00:06:57,374 --> 00:06:59,133
A cloud fills the house.

116
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:05,304
Once a year, on Yom Kippur, the Day of Atonement, only the high priest may enter.

117
00:07:05,304 --> 00:07:08,333
And here the internet adds a famous detail.

118
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:15,759
A rope tied to his ankle, so that if the power of the Ark killed him, the others could drag his body out.

119
00:07:15,759 --> 00:07:20,199
Proof, theorists say, that even the priests feared what was inside.

120
00:07:20,666 --> 00:07:22,121
But check the source.

121
00:07:22,121 --> 00:07:28,840
The rope appears nowhere in the Bible, the Dead Sea Scrolls, Josephus, the Mishnah or the Talmud.

122
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:34,866
Its earliest known mention is the Zohar, a mystical book from thirteenth-century Spain.

123
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:38,572
So what was the Ark, to the people who made it?

124
00:07:38,572 --> 00:07:40,709
Scholars look at its neighbors.

125
00:07:40,709 --> 00:07:48,566
In Egypt, gods traveled in gilded shrines carried on poles by priests, in processions, and sometimes gave oracles.

126
00:07:49,033 --> 00:07:50,813
And we have a real one.

127
00:07:50,813 --> 00:08:00,878
In Tutankhamun's tomb, Howard Carter's team found a gilded wooden chest on long carrying poles, with the jackal god Anubis on top.

128
00:08:00,878 --> 00:08:03,433
A sacred box, made to be carried.

129
00:08:03,899 --> 00:08:07,685
The Bible itself calls the Ark the footstool of God.

130
00:08:07,685 --> 00:08:10,814
The cherubim form an empty throne above it.

131
00:08:10,814 --> 00:08:15,619
Covenant documents were kept at a god's feet in the ancient world.

132
00:08:15,619 --> 00:08:17,293
The design makes sense.

133
00:08:17,293 --> 00:08:18,166
As a shrine.

134
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:30,633
Scholar Scott Noegel argues the best parallel to the Ark is the Egyptian sacred barque, and that the idea probably took shape under Egyptian influence in the Late Bronze Age.

135
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:31,887
Entry six.

136
00:08:31,887 --> 00:08:34,801
The last entry in the log is a blank.

137
00:08:34,801 --> 00:08:40,866
In five hundred eighty-seven B.C., Babylon destroys Jerusalem and its Temple.

138
00:08:41,333 --> 00:08:44,561
The book of Kings lists what was carried off.

139
00:08:44,561 --> 00:08:45,638
Bronze pillars.

140
00:08:45,638 --> 00:08:46,642
Bronze stands.

141
00:08:46,642 --> 00:08:48,149
Pots, shovels, bowls.

142
00:08:48,149 --> 00:08:50,086
The Ark is not on the list.

143
00:08:50,086 --> 00:08:53,100
From here on, the chain of custody breaks.

144
00:08:53,566 --> 00:08:55,314
Tradition fills the gap.

145
00:08:55,314 --> 00:09:00,701
Second Maccabees says the prophet Jeremiah hid it in a cave on Mount Nebo.

146
00:09:00,701 --> 00:09:07,399
Rabbis debated whether it went to Babylon, or whether King Josiah hid it beneath the Temple.

147
00:09:07,866 --> 00:09:18,266
And in Axum, Ethiopia, the Orthodox Church says the Ark is here, in a chapel guarded by a single monk, who never leaves and lets no one see it.

148
00:09:18,733 --> 00:09:26,152
Every Ethiopian Orthodox church keeps a tabot, a replica of the tablets, carried wrapped in procession.

149
00:09:26,152 --> 00:09:33,500
The story of how the Ark came there, the Kebra Nagast, dates in its Ge'ez form to thirteen twenty-one.

150
00:09:33,966 --> 00:09:36,754
One outsider claimed to have seen it.

151
00:09:36,754 --> 00:09:43,838
Edward Ullendorff, a scholar of Ethiopia, said he examined the Axum ark in nineteen forty-one.

152
00:09:43,838 --> 00:09:45,496
A wooden box, he said.

153
00:09:45,496 --> 00:09:45,948
Empty.

154
00:09:45,948 --> 00:09:47,606
Medieval construction.

155
00:09:47,606 --> 00:09:49,866
Nobody has been able to check.

156
00:09:50,333 --> 00:10:01,080
Since twenty seventeen, archaeologists Israel Finkelstein and Thomas Römer have excavated Kiriath Jearim, where the Ark rested for twenty years.

157
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:05,633
They found a monumental platform from the eighth century B.C.

158
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:09,802
They found no Ark, and they were not looking for one.

159
00:10:09,802 --> 00:10:12,735
The chain of custody ends in an empty box.

160
00:10:12,735 --> 00:10:15,180
Which means one thing for our test.

161
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:18,533
Nobody can put the actual object on a lab bench.

162
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,757
But we can test the design.

163
00:10:20,757 --> 00:10:25,639
The theory says: build it to the specification, and it becomes a capacitor.

164
00:10:25,639 --> 00:10:27,266
So let's run the numbers.

165
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:35,306
Gold on both sides of the wood, around five square meters each, with a wooden wall a few centimeters thick.

166
00:10:35,306 --> 00:10:38,633
Our estimate: between three and ten nanofarads.

167
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:42,893
Now charge it to von Däniken's several hundred volts.

168
00:10:42,893 --> 00:10:46,974
The energy stored is less than one thousandth of a joule.

169
00:10:46,974 --> 00:10:52,200
That is weaker than the static spark from a doorknob on a dry winter day.

170
00:10:52,666 --> 00:10:58,306
For comparison, a hospital defibrillator delivers well over a hundred joules.

171
00:10:58,306 --> 00:11:03,432
Safety standards treat discharges above five joules as a serious risk.

172
00:11:03,432 --> 00:11:08,266
The Ark at several hundred volts is thousands of times below that.

173
00:11:08,733 --> 00:11:10,520
Could it be charged higher?

174
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:16,744
To hold five joules, it would need around thirty thousand volts, and something to supply them.

175
00:11:16,744 --> 00:11:20,385
The Bible describes no generator and no lightning rods.

176
00:11:20,385 --> 00:11:23,166
Those were added in the eighteen hundreds.

177
00:11:23,633 --> 00:11:24,772
One last problem.

178
00:11:24,772 --> 00:11:31,943
The gold poles sit in gold rings attached to the outer gold, and the carriers held them on their shoulders.

179
00:11:31,943 --> 00:11:36,366
Any charge on the outside would drain through them as they walked.

180
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:39,938
The radio version fails the same bench.

181
00:11:39,938 --> 00:11:41,212
No power source.

182
00:11:41,212 --> 00:11:42,088
No antenna.

183
00:11:42,088 --> 00:11:43,044
No receiver.

184
00:11:43,044 --> 00:11:49,016
A voice from between the cherubim is how the text describes God's presence.

185
00:11:49,016 --> 00:11:51,166
It is not a wiring diagram.

186
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:53,050
Notice the pattern.

187
00:11:53,050 --> 00:11:57,152
In the age of the Leyden jar, the Ark was a Leyden jar.

188
00:11:57,152 --> 00:11:59,092
In the radio age, a radio.

189
00:11:59,092 --> 00:12:02,896
In the age of science fiction, a weapon from space.

190
00:12:02,896 --> 00:12:06,700
Each era rebuilt the Ark out of its own technology.

191
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:08,791
Chain of custody complete.

192
00:12:08,791 --> 00:12:10,166
Here is the scorecard.

193
00:12:10,633 --> 00:12:14,368
A detailed design survives in Exodus: evidence.

194
00:12:14,368 --> 00:12:18,501
Gold, wood, gold looks like a capacitor: shape only.

195
00:12:18,501 --> 00:12:21,839
It could kill by electric shock: debunked.

196
00:12:21,839 --> 00:12:25,733
The Philistine plague was radiation: no evidence.

197
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:31,957
The high priest's rope proves deadly power: debunked, a medieval legend.

198
00:12:31,957 --> 00:12:36,115
Real Bronze Age parallels exist: evidence, in Egypt.

199
00:12:36,115 --> 00:12:39,633
The Ark was an alien machine: not supported.

200
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:40,945
The verdict.

201
00:12:40,945 --> 00:12:44,044
The machine theory is not an ancient secret.

202
00:12:44,044 --> 00:12:49,398
It is a clever eighteenth-century comparison that grew with every retelling.

203
00:12:49,398 --> 00:12:55,033
Built to its own specification, the Ark is a poor capacitor and no radio at all.

204
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:59,337
What the evidence does support is stranger in its own way.

205
00:12:59,337 --> 00:13:08,466
A people who carried a golden throne for an invisible God at the front of their march, and wrote that its power was holiness, not voltage.

206
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:11,696
Where it is today, nobody can prove.

207
00:13:11,696 --> 00:13:17,222
In Axum, under Jerusalem, in a cave on Mount Nebo, or gone with Babylon.

208
00:13:17,222 --> 00:13:19,754
That part of the case stays open.

209
00:13:19,754 --> 00:13:21,366
Maybe it always will.

210
00:13:21,833 --> 00:13:29,653
But if the Ark is ever found, it will not need to be a machine to be one of the most important discoveries in history.

211
00:13:29,653 --> 00:13:33,166
A wooden box with gold on both sides would be enough.

212
00:13:33,633 --> 00:13:35,292
That is the custody log.

213
00:13:35,292 --> 00:13:37,711
Machine, shrine, or something else?

214
00:13:37,711 --> 00:13:43,033
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery on trial.
